        {
          "path": "_m/r/3/2/0/walhalla-victoria-wp/storm-damn-horseshoe-bend-walh.jpg",
          "filename": "Storm Damn, Horseshoe Bend Walhalla Historic Area Baw Baw National Park.jpg",
          "caption": "This picture was taken on the 19/4/18 at Horseshoe Bend in the Walhalla Historic Area within Baw Baw National Park, Victoria. The shot was taken on a medium format film using my Mamiya RB67 Pro S. I was extremely lucky to have the golden hue as this shot is usually impossible given the sunrise and sunset light doesn't reach this deep inside the valley. Burn-offs in the north meant the sun took on a golden quality through the smoke haze, giving a false twilight all day.",
          "alt": "This picture was taken on the 19/4/18 at Horseshoe Bend in the Walhalla Historic Area within Baw Baw National Park, Victoria. The shot was taken on a medium format film using my Mamiya RB67 Pro S. I was extremely lucky to have the golden hue as this shot is usually impossible given the sunrise and sunset light doesn't reach this deep inside the valley. Burn-offs in the north meant the sun took on a golden quality through the smoke haze, giving a false twilight all day.",
          "width": 2942,
          "height": 2400,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
          "artist": "Maxwellwill9595",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Storm_Damn,_Horseshoe_Bend_Walhalla_Historic_Area_Baw_Baw_National_Park.jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
